Question:
Lattice Federation needs to prevent data loss when its Internet-of-Things (IoT) sensor network experiences periodic traffic spikes while streaming into Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. This state government agency, which monitors public infrastructure sensors across multiple municipalities, relies on continuous telemetry for compliance reporting.
The engineering team notices that the PutRecords API call occasionally fails during these spikes, and the application logs show the following response for a batch write:
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
x-amzn-RequestId: <RequestId>
Content-Type: application/x-amz-json-1.1
Content-Length: <PayloadSizeBytes>
Date: <Date>
 
{
  "FailedRecordCount": 2,
  "Records": [
    {
      "SequenceNumber": "49543463076548007577105092703039560359975228518395012686",
      "ShardId": "shardId-000000000000"
    },
    {
      "ErrorCode": "ProvisionedThroughputExceededException",
      "ErrorMessage": "Rate exceeded for shard shardId-000000000001 in stream exampleStreamName under account 111111111111."
    },
    {
      "ErrorCode": "InternalFailure",
      "ErrorMessage": "Internal service failure."
    }
  ]
}
Which of the following actions should the development team take to resolve this issue? (Select TWO.)

Ashgrove Systems, a theme park operator, has an intern who is new to AWS Cloud and is reviewing an Amazon S3 bucket policy attached to the company's ticketing and reservations account before it moves into wider use. The intern asks a senior Developer Associate to explain what the following policy accomplishes:
{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Sid": "ListAllS3Buckets",
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": ["s3:ListAllMyBuckets"],
            "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::*"
        },
        {
            "Sid": "AllowBucketLevelActions",
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "s3:ListBucket",
                "s3:GetBucketLocation"
            ],
            "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::*"
        },
        {            "Sid": "AllowBucketObjectActions",
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "s3:PutObject",
                "s3:PutObjectAcl",
                "s3:GetObject",
                "s3:GetObjectAcl",
                "s3:DeleteObject"
            ],
            "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::*/*"
        },
        {
            "Sid": "RequireMFAForAshgroveProductionBucket",
            "Effect": "Deny",
            "Action": "s3:*",
            "Resource": [
                "arn:aws:s3:::AshgroveProduction/*",
                "arn:aws:s3:::AshgroveProduction"
            ],
            "Condition": {
                "NumericGreaterThanIfExists": {"aws:MultiFactorAuthAge": "1800"}
            }
        }
    ]
}
What is the best explanation of what this policy does?

